{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788354858,"nonce":"mzZ7uC4J7+hGNWwhELcPzN0FHuo=","message":"**T6's `owners_total` clause was UNREADABLE for the whole of run `m1-20260901`.**\nWorker note, repair round 2026-09-02, filed under `daa269a` acceptance item 5 so\nthat run's own T6 verdict is auditable.\n\nComment #8's thrive table, row T6, requires of a colonist-built barracks:\n\n\u003e `role:\"Barracks\"`, `proper:true`, `open_roof_cells:0`; `beds` count \u003e= roster\n\u003e and **`owners_total` == roster**\n\nOn room 38 every other clause passed and the `owners_total` clause could not\npass, because the field was broken — not because the colony was. `Verse/Room.cs`\n`Owners` takes an early `yield break` when a Barracks has more than one OWNED\nbed, which is exactly room 38's shape (three beds, three distinct owners), so\nthe room-level rollup published `owners_total: 0` beside a `beds[]` block naming\nWouter, Lacey and Jimmy. Nothing threw. See `daa269a` and DESIGN's decisions log\n(`c901f5b`).\n\n**The substitute read the run used, and the one to use for any run graded before\nthis fix landed:** the count of DISTINCT pawn ids across `beds[].owners` in the\nsame `room {id}` envelope. On room 38 that is 3 — Wouter (313), Lacey (310),\nJimmy (323) — one per bed, so **T6 PASSES on room 38** and any FAIL recorded\nagainst it on the `owners_total` clause should be read as a defect in the\ninstrument.\n\nThe failure was silent in the worst way: `owners_total: 0` is also exactly what\nan unassigned barracks reports, and nothing in the envelope could tell the two\napart. Corroboration from outside the verb at the same tick — `digest.colonists`\nread all three as `sleeping. barracks`, and the game had already cleared\n`Alert_NeedColonistBeds` (journal seq 94, tick 12,464).\n\n**Consequence for future gradings.** Per [[acceptance-suites-must-prove-shapes]],\nan assertion of `owners_total == 0` on a fresh room passed for the wrong reason\non any build predating `b5b8c5d`. From that commit the field is derived from\n`ContainedBeds`/`OwnersForReading` and the envelope also carries `beds_total`,\n`beds_owned` and `owners_source`, so a zero is legible: an empty room, unclaimed\nbeds, and a broken rollup are now three distinguishable readings. A grader on the\nnew build can assert `owners_total` directly; a grader replaying a banked\npre-fix envelope must still use the `beds[].owners` substitute.","files":null}]}